WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.330
- When creating business presentations,

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.410
it easily happens that the slides

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:08.230
that you come up with
look like walls of text.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.390
When everything you write

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.760
might be perfectly fine and correct,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.930
just the look of it is boring,

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.260
it's not interesting.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.320
And for sure, this is not what you want

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.300
for your professional presentations.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.000
So when I worked at McKinsey,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.750
we often like to talk about
the look and feel of a slide.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.320
So independent of the content,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.110
what is the look and feel
of what you are creating?

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:30.150
So in today's video,

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.470
I am talking about how you can improve

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.610
the look and feel of your
presentation documents

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.110
by using icons.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.960
So welcome to another coffee break

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.830
here on my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.090
My name is Heinrich
and here on my channel,

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.400
I want to help you to become successful

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.160
in the first years of your career.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.850
I wanna start by saying
thank you to Simple Slides,

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.690
the sponsor of today's video.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.300
Simple Slides is a service

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.050
offering slide templates and infographics,

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.650
I use the service myself

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.250
and can very much recommended it

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.440
but more about that later in the video.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.420
So thank you for joining
me in today's video,

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.940
grab yourself a cup of coffee, as always.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.730
Today I'm just sticking to my water

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.930
because it's already quite late in Germany

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.700
but I hope that you are
having a great time.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.440
So let's now look into a situation

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.440
which I'm facing pretty
much every single day.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.630
And this is, I have a page like this,

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:21.350
so this is a typical text
page, in this example,

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.700
there is a company who
looks into expanding

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.000
into new geographies and new sectors,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.470
and are over here you're summarizing

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:30.130
all the opportunities that
this company might have.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.780
So for instance, geographic
expansion to new countries

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.020
or sector expansion into new sectors.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.890
Now while all of this might
be completely accurate,

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.723
what I write here,

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:42.180
somehow this page seems kind of dull,

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.590
it seems kind of boring,

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:46.970
it's pretty much just a wall of text.

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:49.570
And while it's okay to
have some pages like that

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.600
in your document,

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.230
you do wanna make sure that
not every page looks like this.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:56.560
And indeed, a simple way that you can do

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.800
to improve the look and
feel of a slide like this

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.710
is to use some icons, to
add some icons to your page.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.630
And if you work for a
large consulting firm,

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.410
probably you have libraries of icons,

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.560
libraries of little
infographics to your disposal

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:13.460
that you can use.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.880
But now for the average Joe,

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.820
and probably also for somebody not working

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.820
in these typical consulting firms,

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.830
the access to these
kind of slide libraries

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.190
is much more restricted,

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.650
most companies just do not
have something like this

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:26.483
off the shelf.

00:02:26.483 --> 00:02:28.790
Now of course, what you
can do is to go on Google

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.670
and Google for some icons
there in the picture search.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.190
But here of course, the issue
is that most of the material

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.710
is copyright protected,

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.580
so you cannot just use it
for professional context

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.790
and you just don't wanna use it

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.160
in your business presentations,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.320
even if you're an employee,

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.610
because otherwise you might risk

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.040
that your employer gets
into serious trouble

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.440
if you use these copyright
protected pictures.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.960
So thankfully, there is a service

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.600
that I also use myself
for my presentations,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.450
and this service is called Simple Slides.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:58.700
Simple Slides is a
library of slide templates

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.390
and infographics that
are at your disposal,

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.800
and if you get Simple Slides,

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.630
you can use all the material

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:06.220
for whatever application you want.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.830
So for business and
commercial purposes, as well.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.550
They've over 10,000
slides and infographics

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:12.437
at your disposal

00:03:12.437 --> 00:03:15.140
and the library is
constantly being updated.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.050
Also it doesn't matter
what software you use,

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.950
so whether you use PowerPoint,
Google Slides or Keynote,

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.460
they have material for all
these software packages,

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.180
so you should be covered in either way.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.420
Simple Slides offers
three different tiers.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.260
Personally I have the premium access,

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.660
which gives me access to
all of their materials

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.530
and all of future updates as well.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:34.380
And yes, this is a lifetime access,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.900
so for a one off payment,

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.340
you can use it your whole life.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.110
This is how it looks like on the back end

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.400
once you've opened an account.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.810
And then here on access slides

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.790
you have access to the search bar,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.670
where you can look for whatever you want.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:48.000
So if we type in strategy,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.650
you get different results for that,

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.130
if we type in marketing,

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.790
you get different results for that.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.330
And all of these are search results

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.100
leading to slide packages

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.120
where then you can access

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.480
many different infographics and slides

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:00.900
that fit the individual theme.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.550
But now I am looking for icons

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.400
because I wanna add some icons

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.450
to the PowerPoint presentation.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:07.920
So let's search for icons,

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.270
and you can directly see
that several search results

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.103
are popping up,

00:04:11.103 --> 00:04:13.930
so let's just start by
looking into the vector icons,

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.850
and here they now offer a package

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.660
of all kinds of vector icons

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.770
that you can use for your presentation.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:22.050
So if we now download here
the PowerPoint version,

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.450
it pretty much looks like this.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.220
Now I have opened it here for you guys,

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.000
this is now the package that you get.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.100
So about 14 pages full
of different icon sets

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.200
that you can use for your presentation,

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.720
including also some world
maps, which you can use

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.950
and then also use individual
countries out of it.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.930
So let's now go back and prepare the page

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.420
for adding some icons.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:42.990
So I'm duplicating the page.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.760
Now let's first make some space.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.800
Our goal is to add the
icons to the left here.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.990
So let's make this a little bit smaller.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.200
Let's move this to the right

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.490
and now we have some space

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.320
to add some icons here to the left.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:58.230
So first we have your two
countries, Germany and France,

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.100
and here of course,
now it would make sense

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.290
to get some country icons.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.920
So here now you can click
in and select Germany

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.080
to then get the icon for Germany.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.010
Now it's of course pretty great.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.820
So let's color it in such a nice dark blue

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.160
and we have the first one.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.200
Now let's add the equivalent for France.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.710
Let's insert it this way, color it,

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.860
now we have an icon for France,

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.800
let's make this a little
bit smaller, maybe.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.050
Now it looks good to me,

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.070
let's properly align it, very nice.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:29.870
Now data analysis.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:33.980
So let's just look for what we
could use for data analysis,

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.840
probably something like
this makes a lot of sense.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.310
Let's color it as well.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.070
Now for express services,

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:42.990
probably something like a delivery service

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.730
or parcels or something like that.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.140
This one here looks good to me,

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.500
let's insert it as well, let's color it.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.230
And probably now also another advantage

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.700
of these types of
infographics that you see here

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.110
is that they are vector graphics.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:58.790
So this means that it doesn't
matter how big they are,

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.130
whatever the sizes that you need,

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.580
they will never look out
of resolution, right,

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.130
because the resolution
automatically scales,

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.290
which is of course very comfortable

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.210
when working with them in different sizes.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.770
Let's make this smaller now, here we go.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:16.240
And let's now add this
to the page as well.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.710
Next mining services,

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.880
so probably something with
workshop tools would look nice,

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.160
for instance, something like this.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:27.210
Let's add it, let's
color it, let's insert it

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.330
and here we go.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.180
So now we have it,

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.550
we have icons included in the page

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:33.010
and I hope that you agree

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:35.880
that now this looks a
bit more interesting,

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.730
it's a bit nicer to look at,

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:41.330
the whole presentation looks a
bit less dull if you do this.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.540
So generally, whenever you
have some distinct elements

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:46.200
of your page that you talk about,

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.040
distinct buckets of things,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.200
this is usually always an opportunity

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.690
to include some icons

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:54.760
to make it a little bit
more visually stimulating.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:55.910
What you should avoid, though,

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.380
what I see some people do,

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:59.600
is to only show the icons

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.880
without the explaining text.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.830
So pretty much do something like this,

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:05.920
just here the text and the icons.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.410
This is something I
cannot recommend you to do

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:09.597
because the problem is that

00:07:09.597 --> 00:07:12.970
icons often are not that self explanatory.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:15.740
It often takes quite some
time and mental energy

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:19.460
to interpret what exactly
this or this or this means

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.020
and easily different people

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.390
will have different opinions on that.

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:24.430
There are only very few icons

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:25.410
which are universally

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.020
and interculturally
accepted and recognized.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.460
To use this very carefully,

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:32.350
use icons only to add to an existing name

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.850
but do not only rely
on the power of icons.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:37.440
So when should you and when
should you not use icons

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.800
in your professional
business presentations?

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:42.440
My general recommendation
would be to use them

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.200
but to use them sparsely.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.900
So often a good way to use them

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.970
is if you have some
elements, some opportunities,

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:51.680
some levers, some other buckets of things

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.360
you have in your presentation

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.690
that repeat through all
throughout the slide deck.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:58.370
Because this way you
can establish some icons

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.610
in the beginning on some structure pages

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.940
and to help the reader
to make some connections

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:04.310
among the different pages

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.560
due to the repeating icons that you use.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.270
So applications like this, in my opinion,

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:09.130
make a lot of sense

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.850
because they improve the
look and feel of the pages

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:14.810
and they also have a valuable
benefit for the reader.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:15.910
What you should avoid

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:19.180
is completely spamming your
presentation with icons.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.420
Of course in these business presentations

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:24.400
on almost every page, you
will have an opportunity

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.330
to, in theory, add a
couple of icons to them.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:29.480
But if you add icons to everything,

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.200
they just become meaningless

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:34.130
and at some point it also
looks very repetitive

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:36.310
and also to some extent unprofessional

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:37.690
and childish if you do that.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:39.900
Try to convey meaning via the icons,

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:43.310
try to use them as a true
value add for the reader.

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:44.560
This is the sweet spot

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:46.310
that you should really look out for

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.280
when using icons in your presentations.

